{
 "about": "The 43 asset classes (28 built hubs and 15 linked, unbuilt hub paths) mapped to NAICS. naics2022 is used for County Business Patterns 2023 and QCEW 2025; legacy lists the codes of earlier editions the same businesses carried. SBA FOIA loans carry codes from every edition at once (a 2022 code appears on loans approved in FY1995, and 447110 on loans approved in FY2026), so a loan belongs to a class when its NaicsCode is in any edition list. fit: exact, partial, proxy or none; scripts/markets.py refuses to print a partial or proxy class figure unless the marker states the fit, and never prints a none. Classes are not mutually exclusive (hotel and its four service-level subtypes all use 721110). FOIA loan counts by class, code and edition are measured on every build in naics-evidence.json. Drafted offline by the WEB-FSC-5 mapping subagent from the FOIA code inventory (docs/web-fsc-5/compose/foia_naics_inventory.tsv) and its knowledge of the NAICS editions: the census.gov concordance files are outside the six source hosts, so the edition lists are not checked against a concordance (DECISIONS D13).",
 "aliases": {
  "assisted-living": "assisted-living-and-memory-care",
  "independent-living": "independent-living-and-ccrc",
  "industrial": "industrial-and-warehouse"
 },
